BT 1 0 0 1 0 60 Tm 14 TL .227451 .352941 .196078 rg /F5+0 10 Tf 14 TL (Whatever your child suggests, try to say ) Tj /F6+0 10 Tf 14 TL ("yes, and...") Tj /F5+0 10 Tf 14 TL ( rather than "no". If they want to) Tj T* (befriend the monster, talk to the river, or fly on a borrowed cloud, let them, and add a little) Tj T* (twist that keeps the story moving. "Yes, the vines pull back, and as they do you spot something) Tj T* (glinting underneath." Saying yes keeps a child leaning in. Saying no, again and again, is the) Tj T* (one sure way to lose them.) Tj T* ET
